From 727a89899fd699dd3b40d4e59c87273c239dbebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrik Eriksson <patrik.m.eriksson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:27:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] cdng, rec: APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED chooses when a DNG's
 pages leave the page cache; dropped_copy_slot in the stats line

Why: the writers call posix_fadvise(POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) right after writing a DNG. In Linux 6.12
(mm/fadvise.c) that call starts the file's writeback and then, because the pages are still dirty
or in flight, fails to invalidate them and runs lru_add_drain_all(): work queued on every CPU with
pending LRU batches and waited for, once per frame, freeing almost nothing. The per-frame
sync_file_range that follows finds the writeback already started. The kb's research (working/
dng-chain, R3, R5, R6; verified in V/H3) found this and showed the A1-versus-A2 reading of
2026-10-30 rests on it. cinepi-raw makes no such call. The stop-time stats printed
dropped_copy_slot only when it was above zero, so a clean take could not show the counter was
watched.

What: APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED=writer (default, unchanged), sync (the sync thread drops a cDNG file's
pages after its fsync, when they are clean and the call is cheap) or off; the lossy DNG writer
honours the same knob (no sync thread there, so sync behaves as off). With sync and the sync thread
disabled, Core logs one line. dropped_copy_slot is now a field of the "recording stats" line; the
old separate line is gone.

Tested: the encoders and the whole CameraController.cpp syntax-check (libcamera block on, no new
errors); tools/dng_payload_write_test.sh passes. Reviewed (V/PATCHES.md). Not run on the Pi: the
A/B is A0 against APERTAR_DNG_DONTNEED=sync against =off, 10 minutes each, with Cached from
/proc/meminfo sampled and bpftrace counting lru_add_drain_all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NEFc1zNNwfkFFgzHEzb7wV
